  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_d8a1a688a2264e628b01c29090cba2ce",
      "statement": "The HAAP envelope is a signed JSON object with fields protocol_version, message_type, sender_fingerprint, recipient_fingerprint, timestamp (UTC epoch integer), nonce, payload (object) and signature; PROTOCOL_VERSION is \"1.0\" and envelope_from_bytes rejects any other protocol_version with ProtocolVersionError (wire code PROTOCOL_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/__init__.py#L11-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5acb11e355565769ff5f2bbf8bfe34cc4f3feb99b38adf28f439010229253834:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L153-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47abbf5c4f4bf5bfc10f940a7554fbc4faa3b415185e8adb1f38687a3f77c4b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8257065e53f44b4592963eb4db67ceb3",
      "statement": "canonical_json() produces deterministic signature input: recursively sorted dict keys, compact separators, UTF-8 with ensure_ascii=False, only native JSON values (dict/list/str/int/bool/None); floats are forbidden anywhere in signed data and raise MalformedEnvelopeError, and _check_payload_jsonable enforces the same JSON-only/no-float rule recursively on payloads at signing time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L100-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d9081edc28d8e2f1f679d40f5f2fc9f01b82d4e94e7256152707dba2fb166044:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L61-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:717a351b62fb7300ec039c8bf6d9b976e8957715faf848a30790398965172861:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4b9863c7c00c476093e95849d330f090",
      "statement": "The signature covers the canonical JSON of the entire envelope except the signature key itself (signing_payload drops only \"signature\"), binding sender, recipient, timestamp, nonce, protocol version, message type and payload against field substitution; sign_body validates message_type against MESSAGE_TYPES and payload JSON-ability, generates nonce as base64(secrets.token_bytes(16)) and timestamp from time.time() when omitted, then sets signature to base64 of the Ed25519 signature over signing_payload; envelope_to_bytes serializes the full envelope with canonical_json.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L119-L150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:956fbf93fc3943598d6c19513a9d14deff0bb3147c14755232c82d39b290bfb2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a56854c903914f7fae46fa7ca382be4d",
      "statement": "Timestamps are constrained to a ±300 s window (MAX_CLOCK_SKEW = 300); check_timestamp rejects messages outside now ± 300 s with ClockSkewError (wire code CLOCK_SKEW), and verify_envelope applies this check before public-key lookup and Ed25519 verification so stale messages are discarded without crypto work.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L190-L197",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e104baf594a19e6e7129dbbfbf72c99240ed1c54de940407eb29c3d3a7303dd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L240-L271",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1543197e523fc7d85a2c4a30d0eb19acc251b40b00be0bdb27071c3823a3fd7a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L42-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bae5dbe8df38a69846ac0ac6890a631e3b797f788a246572af3d02b30a526171:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cad4286b26dd43d68f8445d314fa62a4",
      "statement": "NonceManager provides anti-replay keyed on (sender_fingerprint, nonce) pairs: TTL 660 s (2 × MAX_CLOCK_SKEW + 60) with lazy pruning when the cache exceeds MAX_SEEN = 100,000 entries, guarded by a threading.Lock, and a duplicate pair raises ReplayError (wire code NONCE_REPLAY); replays inside the window hit NONCE_REPLAY while replays after 10 minutes fail CLOCK_SKEW, so the mechanism does not depend on the sender's clock.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L200-L237",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:660c30fba61ec95068f33d3c54316a42363c08c6f13dc02d0561e317335a6ef2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_90ee966b45df4d53991b51eabe39f868",
      "statement": "verify_envelope runs the inbound checks in order: structure/version, ±300 s timestamp window, sender public-key lookup by fingerprint in trusted_pubkeys (missing key raises SignatureError, whose wire code BAD_SIGNATURE also covers unknown non-bootstrap senders), fingerprint-to-public-key consistency re-check, Ed25519 verification over signing_payload, and finally nonce marking through the supplied NonceManager so the nonce cache is only polluted by authenticated envelopes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L240-L271",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1543197e523fc7d85a2c4a30d0eb19acc251b40b00be0bdb27071c3823a3fd7a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_279457c6472a4d13beec184f51db9f9b",
      "statement": "HAAPServer.handle_message is the single inbound door for HTTP and in-memory traffic: it re-validates the envelope via envelope_from_bytes(envelope_to_bytes(...)) (a float in a payload therefore surfaces as MALFORMED_ENVELOPE), resolves the sender key through _resolve_sender_pubkey which for bootstrap types (hello, challenge, friend_request, service_search, service_book, service_cancel, service_quote) accepts the payload-declared public key only after checking fingerprint == SHA-256(key), and converts every HAAPError from verification or handlers into a signed error envelope while auditing both accepted and rejected outcomes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L106-L129",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c2339e000445b948a32457fe4789dd352c2a320fe04487e6facfee2c878f7518:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L131-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be05e4fb1055120deb04e264eb10134991bab4d0811e5df615593421f76d7633:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e0532877082d4ac49f4058b421dc8826",
      "statement": "MESSAGE_TYPES is the versioned protocol-1.0 allowlist with exactly: hello, hello_ack, challenge, verify, friend_request, friend_accept, capabilities, task_request, task_accept, task_result, task_progress, error, ping, service_search, service_quote, service_book, service_cancel (the service_* marketplace types are signed open-service requests that need no prior friendship); the allowlist is enforced both by sign_body (refuses unknown types) and by envelope_from_bytes (rejects unknown inbound types before any handler runs).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/envelope.py#L132-L133",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:87f0492bddfb5a514d7d60220d6c97b3eba06b0f7f08e533793044ae9755dcd3:"
