    {
      "id": "claim_3315d043baa741809700fe90627c5388",
      "statement": "The HTTP layer only returns HTTP 400 with a truncated error for faults before any cryptographic check (JSON that envelope_from_bytes cannot parse); a parsed envelope always gets HTTP 200 with the reply envelope (including signed error envelopes), and an empty reply returns HTTP 202, so envelope-level failures never masquerade as transport errors.",
      "evidence": [
