    {
      "id": "claim_0cc0088ec0b549c983edee2333ae7d46",
      "statement": "errors.py defines the stable on-wire code catalog: HAAP_ERROR, PROTOCOL_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED, BAD_SIGNATURE, UNKNOWN_SENDER, CLOCK_SKEW, NONCE_REPLAY, MALFORMED_ENVELOPE, CHALLENGE_REQUIRED, NOT_INITIALIZED, FRIEND_NOT_FOUND, FRIEND_BLOCKED, FRIEND_NOT_ACCEPTED, DUPLICATE_REQUEST, PERMISSION_DENIED, RATE_LIMITED (transient with retry_after), TRANSPORT_ERROR (transient with HTTP status), DISCOVERY_FAILED, TASK_ERROR, TASK_NOT_FOUND, TASK_STATE_INVALID, TASK_LIMIT_REACHED (transient with retry_after), UNEXPECTED_MESSAGE and FRIEND_REQUEST_DENIED; ERROR_MAP maps every code to its exception class and error_from_code instantiates the exception for a received code, degrading unknown codes to a generic HAAPError.",
